# Gemma Compute Monitor — frontend environment template.
# Copy to frontend/.env.local for local dev; on Railway, set the same two
# variables as service environment variables. Do NOT commit real values.
#
# IMPORTANT — NEXT_PUBLIC_* semantics:
# Variables prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ are inlined into the client JavaScript bundle
# at BUILD time by Next.js. They are therefore NOT secret and ARE visible in the
# browser. The password below is a lightweight shared-access gate, NOT real
# authentication (multi-user sessions and backend auth are out of scope).
# Because these values are baked in at build time, changing NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL
# requires a Railway rebuild/redeploy to take effect — this is exactly step (c)
# of the per-session ngrok workflow described in COMPUTE_MONITOR.md.
#
# dotenv syntax: KEY=value, one per line, no spaces around '=' on active
# entries, and comments start with '#'.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED — backend API base URL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED. Base URL of the local FastAPI backend, exposed to the public
# frontend through an ngrok HTTPS tunnel (`ngrok http 8000`). The client uses it
# for GET {NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/health and POST {NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/analyze.
# Use the HTTPS URL with NO trailing slash (the client joins the paths itself).
# It MUST be reachable over HTTPS from the public Railway origin: a plain-http
# backend called from an https page is blocked by the browser as mixed content,
# which is why the ngrok HTTPS tunnel is required. On free ngrok the subdomain
# changes every session, so each new session ends with a Railway redeploy to
# pick up the new URL. For local-only dev against a locally running backend you
# may instead use http://localhost:8000.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://YOUR-NGROK-SUBDOMAIN.ngrok-free.app

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED — shared access password
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED. The single shared password the frontend gate
# (components/PasswordGate.tsx) compares against the value persisted in the
# browser's localStorage. This is NOT real authentication — it is a lightweight
# shared-access gate. Choose any non-empty string for the deployment.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PASSWORD=change-me
